<P>
The particular strains selected were ones that survived refrigeration well and provided 

reproducible data using the VITEK&#174; system.  Eight VITEK&#174; Test Cards were placed 

into each VITEK&#174; Card Tray.  Six trays were used for this experiment containing a total 

of 48 cards.  (For specific VITEK&#174; Test Card well components, see the STS-107 hardware 

configuration for the AMS).  Yeast species were in a nitrogen-based medium, unless otherwise 

noted.  
<P>
Ground activities included performing identical studies using the same test isolates in the 

training hardware concurrently with the inflight experiment.  Parallel AMS evaluation of 

identical VITEK&#174; Test Cards were done at the same time the inflight experiments were 

run.
<P>
Preflight activities included preparation and inoculation of the VITEK&#174; Test Cards 

followed by transfer to the Shuttle&#39;s refrigerator called the Thermoelectric Holding 

Module (TEHM).  
<P>
Flight day one (FD1) operations consisted of activation of the AMS and set up of the Laptop 

Experiment Computer System (LECS).  The first VITEK&#174; Card Tray was removed from the 

TEHM and transferred to the AMS for analysis.  A check was performed 20 minutes after start 

of incubation cycle to verify temperature and check for errors.  An incubation cycle 

consisted of a ten minute wait period followed by a five minute read cycle.    On FD2-FD7:  

the AMS status was checked, data was saved, analyzed VITEK&#174; Card Trays were transferred 

from the AMS to the TEHM, new VITEK&#174; Card Trays were transferred from the TEHM to the 

AMS, AMS filter was cleaned, and the status was verified after one cycle.  All trays for 

this experiment were incubated for 24 hours &#177; 4 hours in the AMS, so these activities 

occurred daily with the last tray being removed on FD7.  The other MPFE experiment&#39;s 

VITEK&#174; Card Trays were processed on FD7 through FD11.  The AMS was deactivated and all 

other hardware was stowed on FD11.
<P>
Postflight activities were to include transfer of the VITEK&#174; Card Trays with cards, and 

data from the Shuttle to the investigators for analysis.  
<P>
<B>Results:</B><BR>
Due to the STS-107 tragedy, this experiment was not completed.
